<!--META-DATA
{
	tags: for, indexing,
}
-->

<statement>
<p>
	This program returns an AI move to an available space in a Tic-Tac-Toe game based on your chosen strategy.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Inputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>game_state</pf> (3 x 3) number — the current state of the TTT game board</p>
			<p><pf>player</pf> (1 x 1) number — has value <pf>1</pf> if X is the current player or <pf>-1</pf> if O is the current player.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Outputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>move_to</pf> (1 x 1) integer — absolute index of the space <pf>player</pf> should move to.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>Your grade on this program will be based on how well it does, on average, when played head-to-head against the</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>TTT_ai_move_2</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>strategy.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>I will simulate 1000 games against your code and the</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>TTT_ai_move_2</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>strategy. Half of the games your code will have the first move.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Do not look up strategies online or ask anyone for help on this one. You should own it completely.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

</statement>
